WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.760
An old story says a
river fell from heaven,

2
00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:07.920
and a god caught her so her fall
would not shatter the earth.

3
00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:14.060
Today that river flows past Varanasi,
where pilgrims step into the water at dawn.

4
00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:18.540
Others travel to mountains and towns
linked with the lives of the gods.

5
00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:21.590
Yet many Hindus believe God is everywhere,

6
00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:24.060
even in the heart and the home shrine.

7
00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:26.540
So why make the journey at all?

8
00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:30.390
In this mission, you'll visit
Varanasi and other pilgrim sites,

9
00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:32.300
and see what pilgrims do.

10
00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:37.130
Then you'll compare how followers of
Vishnu and Shiva see sacred places,

11
00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:40.180
and weigh up whether
pilgrimage still matters.

12
00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:45.010
Your mission: find out why a journey
to a river can matter so much.
